WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.622
- When you're trying to make

00:00:02.622 --> 00:00:07.023
something which is new
and bold and dangerous,

00:00:07.023 --> 00:00:08.626
you risk going too far.

00:00:08.626 --> 00:00:09.810
You know, I was always around rugby.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.762
I was playing at quite a high level.

00:00:11.762 --> 00:00:15.233
I can't stand watching Thrones
and knowing it's a stuntman

00:00:15.233 --> 00:00:17.954
that's doing my bit, so anytime,

00:00:17.954 --> 00:00:19.508
you know, I can, I want to do the stunt.

00:00:19.508 --> 00:00:21.739
I had been in a fight the night before.

00:00:21.739 --> 00:00:25.067
I'd gotten in this fight
with this guy in McDonald's.

00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:25.900
- What's up, Believe Nation?

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.241
It's Evan, my one word is believe,

00:00:28.241 --> 00:00:29.967
and I believe that you have the ability

00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:32.756
to do something special
that can change the planet.

00:00:32.756 --> 00:00:33.589
To help you on your journey,

00:00:33.589 --> 00:00:34.679
today we're going to learn from one of the

00:00:34.679 --> 00:00:37.632
highest paid actors on TV, Kit Harrington,

00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:40.472
and my take on his top
10 rules of success.

00:00:40.472 --> 00:00:42.167
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:42.167 --> 00:00:43.188
and I'd love to know which one

00:00:43.188 --> 00:00:45.105
you guys like the best.

00:00:47.659 --> 00:00:50.242
(upbeat music)

00:00:57.935 --> 00:01:00.586
- I think unless we are

00:01:00.586 --> 00:01:04.753
pushing the boundaries of what
we are comfortable viewing,

00:01:05.778 --> 00:01:08.028
we're not making art,

00:01:09.353 --> 00:01:12.853
and I think that's why Game of Thrones is,

00:01:14.422 --> 00:01:16.791
people have responded so,

00:01:16.791 --> 00:01:18.857
so much to Game of Thrones, is that they,

00:01:18.857 --> 00:01:22.006
they're watching something
which shocks them,

00:01:22.006 --> 00:01:25.156
which moves them, which
makes them scared or angry.

00:01:25.156 --> 00:01:28.032
I think the thing that
you risk is you can,

00:01:28.032 --> 00:01:30.511
when you're trying to make

00:01:30.511 --> 00:01:34.741
something which is new
and bold and dangerous,

00:01:34.741 --> 00:01:36.254
you risk going too far.

00:01:36.254 --> 00:01:38.193
You're always going to take that risk.

00:01:38.193 --> 00:01:42.779
In Thrones, I think we
have gone too far at times,

00:01:42.779 --> 00:01:46.628
and in Doctor Faustus, we definitely did.

00:01:46.628 --> 00:01:51.143
It didn't work in some ways
because it was too much.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:55.193
But I think unless you try,
you're not pushing boundaries.

00:01:55.193 --> 00:01:56.901
You're not making art.

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:59.033
I had a few moments during Game of Thrones

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:02.293
where you're very into it and very

00:02:02.293 --> 00:02:04.795
kind of concentrating on what you're doing

00:02:04.795 --> 00:02:06.144
and constantly trying to improve

00:02:06.144 --> 00:02:08.415
and get it better and better.

00:02:08.415 --> 00:02:10.635
Every now and again, you have a moment.

00:02:10.635 --> 00:02:11.967
I had a couple where

00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:15.473
it was just on set in
this cloak with this sword

00:02:15.473 --> 00:02:18.190
and this amazing castle that they built.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:20.518
You just kind of go this is really cool.

00:02:20.518 --> 00:02:21.563
This is just cool,

00:02:21.563 --> 00:02:23.451
and this is what I became an actor to do,

00:02:23.451 --> 00:02:26.114
is to live this kind of world.

00:02:26.114 --> 00:02:27.286
It's every young actor's dream

00:02:27.286 --> 00:02:30.040
to play those parts where
you're a badass sword fighter.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.822
- [Interviewer] Well you
see, and if the kids dream.

00:02:31.822 --> 00:02:32.655
- Yeah!

00:02:32.655 --> 00:02:34.523
Yeah, I've read the books.

00:02:34.523 --> 00:02:36.690
The minute I got the part,

00:02:37.922 --> 00:02:40.830
I went and bought all
of them and read them,

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:44.805
mainly out of curiosity about
what might be happening.

00:02:44.805 --> 00:02:48.456
Also, out of I felt I had
a source material there.

00:02:48.456 --> 00:02:49.942
Whenever I've got a source material,

00:02:49.942 --> 00:02:51.745
I feel that it, for me anyway,

00:02:51.745 --> 00:02:53.953
I need to look at all information

00:02:53.953 --> 00:02:55.542
I can gather about that
fictional character.

00:02:55.542 --> 00:02:56.638
The first description,

00:02:56.638 --> 00:02:58.777
if you read the first description of Jon,

00:02:58.777 --> 00:03:02.520
it informed, I think I, I
think I, for my audition,

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.443
I bought the book, read the
first description of Jon,

00:03:05.443 --> 00:03:08.204
read a bit to get an idea of it,

00:03:08.204 --> 00:03:09.674
and then went in with that.

00:03:09.674 --> 00:03:12.879
It's already in the book that he's quiet,

00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:15.877
he's quite sort of

00:03:15.877 --> 00:03:17.294
dower in a way.

00:03:18.356 --> 00:03:20.676
He's like the black sheep in the family.

00:03:20.676 --> 00:03:23.165
When that first paragraph about who he was

00:03:23.165 --> 00:03:26.327
and what his sort of essence was like,

00:03:26.327 --> 00:03:28.882
gave me that first sort
of tap into how I should,

00:03:28.882 --> 00:03:32.272
how I should do that first audition.

00:03:32.272 --> 00:03:33.601
Then that template stays with you

00:03:33.601 --> 00:03:36.763
for six years of what
character you've made.

00:03:36.763 --> 00:03:38.214
That's the way I,

00:03:38.214 --> 00:03:40.292
if I have something like that to go on,

00:03:40.292 --> 00:03:41.831
the way I work.

00:03:41.831 --> 00:03:44.595
I'll look at exactly what
the writer or these writers

00:03:44.595 --> 00:03:47.460
or the writer of the book
thinks this person is

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.288
and try and tell that story.

00:03:49.288 --> 00:03:52.201
- Did you ever try your hand at football?

00:03:52.201 --> 00:03:54.068
- I was a rugby player when I was young.

00:03:54.068 --> 00:03:54.901
- Rugby?

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.461
- Yeah, I was a scrum-half.

00:03:56.461 --> 00:03:58.410
A scrum-half's the little guy.

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.612
He's the smallest guy on the rugby team.

00:04:00.612 --> 00:04:03.189
Scrappy, yeah, he's hard to catch.

00:04:03.189 --> 00:04:05.542
He takes the ball out of the scrum-half

00:04:05.542 --> 00:04:08.893
and he gets it's out to the backs.

00:04:08.893 --> 00:04:10.296
The back line, you might say.

00:04:10.296 --> 00:04:11.976
- [Rich] So did you realize early on

00:04:11.976 --> 00:04:14.760
that perhaps acting was the
better way for you to go?

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:15.593
Is that what you're saying?

00:04:15.593 --> 00:04:17.020
- I remember the tackle that did it, yeah.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.814
- What was that?

00:04:18.814 --> 00:04:20.069
- You know, I was around rugby.

00:04:20.069 --> 00:04:22.640
I was playing at quite a high level,

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.179
but there's something
that happens to young men

00:04:24.179 --> 00:04:27.596
when they go from being 16, 17, years old

00:04:28.765 --> 00:04:31.282
to suddenly, I was
playing at 18 years old.

00:04:31.282 --> 00:04:34.885
You know when young men go
from being young men to men.

00:04:34.885 --> 00:04:37.442
I remember the time I
got hit with a tackle.

00:04:37.442 --> 00:04:39.438
I was in the drama
society at the same time

00:04:39.438 --> 00:04:42.344
as being on the rugby team.

00:04:42.344 --> 00:04:45.435
I thought, "I got to protect this."

00:04:45.435 --> 00:04:46.422
- [Rich] The money maker.

00:04:46.422 --> 00:04:48.229
- Got to protect the money maker.

00:04:48.229 --> 00:04:51.220
One more hit like that to my face,

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.480
I can kiss acting goodbye.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.920
- How physically demanding
is your role on the show,

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.091
and how has it differed from other roles?

00:04:57.091 --> 00:04:58.076
You do your own stunts.

00:04:58.076 --> 00:04:59.303
Do you do your own stunts?

00:04:59.303 --> 00:05:00.136
- Yeah, I do.

00:05:00.136 --> 00:05:01.382
- [Interviewer] Have you ever gotten hurt?

00:05:01.382 --> 00:05:03.664
- Yeah, you get knocks and
bruises, nothing major.

00:05:03.664 --> 00:05:04.497
You have to have physio--

00:05:04.497 --> 00:05:05.521
- [Interviewer] You've never
broken your nose or anything?

00:05:05.521 --> 00:05:08.118
- No, no, not the nose, darling.

00:05:08.118 --> 00:05:09.335
- [Interviewer] (laughs)

00:05:09.335 --> 00:05:10.677
Watch the face, watch the face!

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:12.921
- Watch the face.

00:05:12.921 --> 00:05:15.041
No, I, knocks and bruises.

00:05:15.041 --> 00:05:19.682
I've done far worst things
to myself on my own time.

00:05:19.682 --> 00:05:20.515
I like doing it.

00:05:20.515 --> 00:05:23.708
I can't stand watching Thrones
and knowing it's a stuntman

00:05:23.708 --> 00:05:26.283
that's doing my bit, so anytime,

00:05:26.283 --> 00:05:27.982
you know, I can, I want to do the stunt.

00:05:27.982 --> 00:05:29.687
Every now and again, it
has to be a stuntman,

00:05:29.687 --> 00:05:30.974
but usually, it's me.

00:05:30.974 --> 00:05:32.015
Usually, it's me.

00:05:32.015 --> 00:05:35.235
- I imagine it's kind of
terrifying, I imagine.

00:05:35.235 --> 00:05:39.194
Acting on stage in front of an
audience every single night.

00:05:39.194 --> 00:05:40.818
- It is, but that's the reason,

00:05:40.818 --> 00:05:42.758
I think, any actor gets into it,

00:05:42.758 --> 00:05:45.056
or any actor who starts
on the stage, especially.

00:05:45.056 --> 00:05:46.290
You get into it for that kind

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:49.925
of thrill-seeking reason in some ways,

00:05:49.925 --> 00:05:51.592
the adrenaline rush.

00:05:53.313 --> 00:05:54.146
I love it.

00:05:54.146 --> 00:05:56.378
I forgot what live
performance was for a while

00:05:56.378 --> 00:05:58.036
and now I'm really enjoying it.

00:05:58.036 --> 00:05:58.904
- This particularly,

00:05:58.904 --> 00:06:02.748
this role in Pompeii was
hard right, physically tough?

00:06:02.748 --> 00:06:05.901
- Yeah, I mean, when I
got into it, I sort of,

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:08.014
I looked at it and knew I
was playing a gladiator.

00:06:08.014 --> 00:06:10.921
I thought I better look
like a gladiator, right?

00:06:10.921 --> 00:06:12.190
I said to the director,

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:13.605
"I would really like do kind of a

00:06:13.605 --> 00:06:15.243
"body transformation thing for this.

00:06:15.243 --> 00:06:16.772
"It's something that I've wanted to do

00:06:16.772 --> 00:06:18.059
"for awhile for a part."

00:06:18.059 --> 00:06:19.690
- Like the Quick Trim 50-day challenge

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:22.521
or something like that
or more of a gym thing?

00:06:22.521 --> 00:06:25.106
- I wanted to, you know,

00:06:25.106 --> 00:06:27.304
if you do some research about gladiators,

00:06:27.304 --> 00:06:28.571
they did look like...

00:06:28.571 --> 00:06:29.533
- [Kyle] Monsters?

00:06:29.533 --> 00:06:30.366
They're huge, right?

00:06:30.366 --> 00:06:33.192
- Huge, very, very cut,
very, very, chiseled.

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:35.429
- How long did you have to
transform your body that way?

00:06:35.429 --> 00:06:37.703
- I had about five weeks.

00:06:37.703 --> 00:06:38.715
- [Jackie] Ooh, that's not long.

00:06:38.715 --> 00:06:39.918
- It's not long.

00:06:39.918 --> 00:06:41.849
- [Jackie] What was involved then?

00:06:41.849 --> 00:06:44.279
- I wouldn't be able to
lose one kilo in five weeks.

00:06:44.279 --> 00:06:46.875
- I put on 10 kilos

00:06:46.875 --> 00:06:49.569
in five, in four weeks,

00:06:49.569 --> 00:06:51.680
and then I had to in another three weeks,

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.170
I had to, while we
started filming the film,

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.945
I had to cut down those 10 kilos again.

00:06:56.945 --> 00:07:00.797
So, I put on 10 kilos
and then lost 10 kilos.

00:07:00.797 --> 00:07:02.448
By that time, you keep all the muscle,

00:07:02.448 --> 00:07:03.866
but you just sort of, um...

00:07:03.866 --> 00:07:04.710
- You carve yourself up.

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.213
You look like a gladiator.

00:07:06.213 --> 00:07:07.773
- And when you're doing
those fight scenes,

00:07:07.773 --> 00:07:08.899
which would be pretty intense,

00:07:08.899 --> 00:07:11.455
how long is the filming on those?

00:07:11.455 --> 00:07:12.288
- Long.

00:07:12.288 --> 00:07:13.121
- Long?

00:07:13.121 --> 00:07:13.954
- Long, yeah it's--

00:07:13.954 --> 00:07:15.037
- It's hours.

00:07:16.145 --> 00:07:18.556
- If you're not doing the
fight scenes, filming them,

00:07:18.556 --> 00:07:21.547
you're in a room training
for the next one.

00:07:21.547 --> 00:07:25.831
The director we have, Paul,
the director, he basically

00:07:25.831 --> 00:07:27.207
said, he would come in

00:07:27.207 --> 00:07:30.883
and we'd have choreographed
about 10 fights,

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:32.812
you know, to show him.

00:07:32.812 --> 00:07:36.897
Then he'd come in and say, "No,
I don't like any of those."

00:07:36.897 --> 00:07:39.106
When they've taken you
like five weeks to learn.

00:07:39.106 --> 00:07:41.231
- And you're like, Jesus.

00:07:41.231 --> 00:07:43.173
- He said that that's not,
I don't like that one.

00:07:43.173 --> 00:07:44.006
I don't like that.

00:07:44.006 --> 00:07:46.008
So, you'd have to go
and relearn a whole bit.

00:07:46.008 --> 00:07:48.213
By the end of it, you can pick
up a fight pretty quickly.

00:07:48.213 --> 00:07:50.268
- Do you worry that you'll get typecasted

00:07:50.268 --> 00:07:51.473
with the Game of Thrones,
you know what I mean?

00:07:51.473 --> 00:07:53.052
'Cause it is, I mean,

00:07:53.052 --> 00:07:56.727
the cast is so imprinted
on everyone's imagination

00:07:56.727 --> 00:07:59.778
that people thing you are Jon Snow.

00:07:59.778 --> 00:08:00.842
- There is that worry.

00:08:00.842 --> 00:08:01.877
There is that idea,

00:08:01.877 --> 00:08:04.984
will I ever break away
from this character?

00:08:04.984 --> 00:08:08.437
When I wanted to get into
acting, I wanted to just work.

00:08:08.437 --> 00:08:11.909
I wanted to work as an actor to do,

00:08:11.909 --> 00:08:12.833
to act.

00:08:12.833 --> 00:08:15.596
It's just is an honor in itself.

00:08:15.596 --> 00:08:17.788
This enables me to do that.

00:08:17.788 --> 00:08:20.705
This may be a defining role for me,

00:08:21.556 --> 00:08:25.072
but it's going to allow me
to do lots of other things.

00:08:25.072 --> 00:08:27.471
I don't worry about
that typecasting issue.

00:08:27.471 --> 00:08:28.357
I always think people,

00:08:28.357 --> 00:08:30.850
other people worry about
it too much for me.

00:08:30.850 --> 00:08:33.636
I'm like, I don't, I
don't see it as a problem.

00:08:33.636 --> 00:08:34.760
- The first time Kit walked into the room,

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:39.175
I remember thinking, "Oh,
please let this guy be good."

00:08:39.175 --> 00:08:40.642
I just have an image in my mind,

00:08:40.642 --> 00:08:42.571
with most of the characters
I don't, but with Jon Snow,

00:08:42.571 --> 00:08:44.460
I had an image in my
mind of what he should,

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:45.761
not only what he should look like,

00:08:45.761 --> 00:08:47.566
but more what he should kind of feel like,

00:08:47.566 --> 00:08:51.920
a certain burning intensity
and a kind of haunted thing.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.722
(audience laughs)

00:08:53.722 --> 00:08:54.555
So, he comes in.

00:08:54.555 --> 00:08:55.735
- Do it, do it.

00:08:55.735 --> 00:08:56.873
- Do blue steel.

00:08:56.873 --> 00:08:57.829
- [Man] Blue steel.

00:08:57.829 --> 00:08:59.242
Brood steel.

00:08:59.242 --> 00:09:02.742
- That was just definitely something else.

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:04.686
- He came in and he nailed it.

00:09:04.686 --> 00:09:06.358
He was just, he was incredible.

00:09:06.358 --> 00:09:09.025
(intense music)

00:09:13.047 --> 00:09:15.628
- I've really admired his work.

00:09:15.628 --> 00:09:17.712
I had seen him as Jon Snow

00:09:17.712 --> 00:09:20.477
and I knew that this was
a very different part.

00:09:20.477 --> 00:09:21.352
He just came in, well,

00:09:21.352 --> 00:09:24.185
we met at the reading,
and he just blew me away.

00:09:24.185 --> 00:09:25.937
He brings such, you know,

00:09:25.937 --> 00:09:28.708
a strong heart and intelligent performance

00:09:28.708 --> 00:09:30.370
and yet, very sensitive.

00:09:30.370 --> 00:09:33.091
- It's nice when you get
to work with a friend,

00:09:33.091 --> 00:09:36.091
and you know, and it actually works,

00:09:37.077 --> 00:09:39.432
'cause the other way is not fun.

00:09:39.432 --> 00:09:42.015
I've had a scene I had to play.

00:09:45.042 --> 00:09:46.542
Sorry, one second.

00:09:47.453 --> 00:09:49.536
I think probably,

00:09:51.629 --> 00:09:53.667
it was probably the,

00:09:53.667 --> 00:09:54.719
there was this scene.

00:09:54.719 --> 00:09:55.886
Okay, so it...

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.874
It was the scene with um...

00:09:59.874 --> 00:10:00.707
When

00:10:01.644 --> 00:10:03.328
Ygritte dies.

00:10:03.328 --> 00:10:05.320
It was so sad.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:08.506
We had three weeks of night shoots,

00:10:08.506 --> 00:10:11.673
so everyone was very emotional anyway.

00:10:14.007 --> 00:10:15.257
The scene where

00:10:16.703 --> 00:10:20.389
I turn around and she's
there with the arrow.

00:10:20.389 --> 00:10:23.307
It was this moment of like,

00:10:23.307 --> 00:10:24.724
well, it's funny.

00:10:25.627 --> 00:10:28.595
I turned around and smiled because,

00:10:28.595 --> 00:10:31.691
I didn't mean to, I just did.

00:10:31.691 --> 00:10:35.274
Then that seemed to
work, so we kept it in.

00:10:36.296 --> 00:10:39.213
(breathes heavily)

00:10:44.342 --> 00:10:47.175
(sorrowful music)

00:11:01.054 --> 00:11:03.221
(gurgles)

00:11:09.895 --> 00:11:12.126
- Jon Snow.

00:11:12.126 --> 00:11:13.399
- Hush.

00:11:13.399 --> 00:11:14.330
Don't talk.

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:17.163
(sorrowful music)

00:11:19.287 --> 00:11:21.370
- You remember that cave?

00:11:26.252 --> 00:11:29.169
We should have stayed in that cave.

00:11:32.876 --> 00:11:34.709
- We'll go back there.

00:11:40.872 --> 00:11:43.789
- You know nothing, Jon Snow.

00:12:12.232 --> 00:12:13.430
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:16.730
I made this video because
Ivan on my team asked me too.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:20.199
Ivan does most of the research
behind all of these videos,

00:12:20.199 --> 00:12:22.813
so I had to do him a
solid and make this video.

00:12:22.813 --> 00:12:23.646
If there's someone you'd like

00:12:23.646 --> 00:12:25.374
to vote on for the next Top 10,

00:12:25.374 --> 00:12:26.826
check out the link in the description,

00:12:26.826 --> 00:12:28.443
and go and have your say.

00:12:28.443 --> 00:12:30.957
Finally, I want to give a
quick shout out to BestYouPro.

00:12:30.957 --> 00:12:32.965
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:12:32.965 --> 00:12:33.798
Your One Word,

00:12:33.798 --> 00:12:35.168
and taking that amazing picture

00:12:35.168 --> 00:12:37.191
of you on the beach reading it.

00:12:37.191 --> 00:12:38.987
I'm so glad you enjoyed the book,

00:12:38.987 --> 00:12:40.365
and I really appreciate your support.

00:12:40.365 --> 00:12:41.758
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:12:41.758 --> 00:12:42.936
I believe in you.

00:12:42.936 --> 00:12:44.788
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:12:44.788 --> 00:12:48.332
and whatever your one word is, much love.

00:12:48.332 --> 00:12:49.832
I'll see you soon.

00:12:55.254 --> 00:12:57.847
- I'm playing a cowboy at the moment.

00:12:57.847 --> 00:13:00.347
I've got to do loads
of things that kids do,

00:13:00.347 --> 00:13:03.347
like I got to be a medieval warrior.

00:13:04.197 --> 00:13:06.293
I got to be a cowboy.

00:13:06.293 --> 00:13:07.626
I've been a spy.

00:13:09.165 --> 00:13:11.150
I've been a gladiator.

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:13.205
I've got to play around, man.

00:13:13.205 --> 00:13:14.038
It was a lot of fun.

00:13:14.038 --> 00:13:15.734
- I do remember the audition for Jon Snow.

00:13:15.734 --> 00:13:18.004
I had a black eye.

00:13:18.004 --> 00:13:20.061
I'd been in a if hgt the night before.

00:13:20.061 --> 00:13:23.408
I'd gotten in this fight
with this guy in McDonald's.

00:13:23.408 --> 00:13:24.496
I went into the McDonald's

00:13:24.496 --> 00:13:27.518
with this girl I was sort
of dating at the time.

00:13:27.518 --> 00:13:29.940
It was late at night,
and there was no seats.

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:31.658
I asked this,

00:13:31.658 --> 00:13:32.949
this guy and this girl

00:13:32.949 --> 00:13:34.516
he was with if we could
sit on the same table

00:13:34.516 --> 00:13:36.124
as them and they said yes.

00:13:36.124 --> 00:13:36.957
We sat down.

00:13:36.957 --> 00:13:38.011
Quite quickly, he
started being really rude

00:13:38.011 --> 00:13:40.335
to the girl I was with, calling her names.

00:13:40.335 --> 00:13:41.813
We were like, we'll just finish our food,

00:13:41.813 --> 00:13:43.554
we don't need trouble, and then go.

00:13:43.554 --> 00:13:44.461
Then he called her something like

00:13:44.461 --> 00:13:46.425
an ugly pig or something worse.

00:13:46.425 --> 00:13:48.930
I got up and said, "No, no, no, you can't.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:49.781
"You can't call her that.

00:13:49.781 --> 00:13:50.614
"Get up."

00:13:50.614 --> 00:13:51.796
So I called him out for a fight,

00:13:51.796 --> 00:13:52.629
which I've never done before.

00:13:52.629 --> 00:13:54.308
Of course, he'd been
sat down the whole time.

00:13:54.308 --> 00:13:57.814
He got up and he just kept going.

00:13:57.814 --> 00:13:59.617
I just realized

00:13:59.617 --> 00:14:01.797
that I had to, at that
point, throw the first punch.

00:14:01.797 --> 00:14:03.490
Otherwise, I'd look like a complete wimp.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:04.864
I got battered.

00:14:04.864 --> 00:14:07.877
Then, I went to the Jon Snow
audition with a black eye,

00:14:07.877 --> 00:14:09.639
which I think that man
who punched me in the face

00:14:09.639 --> 00:14:10.874
may have helped me get the job,

00:14:10.874 --> 00:14:12.677
so if you're watching, thank you.

00:14:12.677 --> 00:14:14.086
Very soon after the,

00:14:14.086 --> 00:14:17.405
the show had aired, and I was dead.

00:14:17.405 --> 00:14:19.631
There was a lot of questions
about whether I'd come back,

00:14:19.631 --> 00:14:21.860
and that cliffhanger had just started.

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:24.193
The policeman pulled me over

00:14:25.576 --> 00:14:26.659
for speeding.

00:14:29.244 --> 00:14:32.425
I got pulled over and he said,

00:14:32.425 --> 00:14:33.674
"We can take you into the office

00:14:33.674 --> 00:14:35.337
"and we can give you a
fine and give you points

00:14:35.337 --> 00:14:37.593
"or you can tell me whether you live

00:14:37.593 --> 00:14:38.940
"in the next season of Game of Thrones."

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.190
- [Interviewer] Oh my gosh.

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:41.040
- I know.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:41.992
- [Interviewer] How outrageous.

00:14:41.992 --> 00:14:43.723
- And I thought, you know, this is a joke.

00:14:43.723 --> 00:14:46.896
This must be a joke and
he was deadly serious.

00:14:46.896 --> 00:14:48.111
I said, "Well, I'm,

00:14:48.111 --> 00:14:49.524
"I'm alive."

00:14:49.524 --> 00:14:51.406
Then he says, "On your
way, Lord Commander."

00:14:51.406 --> 00:14:52.239
- No way.

00:14:52.239 --> 00:14:53.156
- It was just fantastic, isn't it?

00:14:53.156 --> 00:14:54.807
I love that police officer.

00:14:54.807 --> 00:14:56.872
The only thing better than
being alive in reality

00:14:56.872 --> 00:14:58.741
is being alive fictionally as well.

00:14:58.741 --> 00:15:01.559
We did thousands upon thousands of takes

00:15:01.559 --> 00:15:03.296
'cause it's such a key moment, I think,

00:15:03.296 --> 00:15:05.047
of me going (gasps) like that,

00:15:05.047 --> 00:15:07.286
that they wanted that over and over again.

00:15:07.286 --> 00:15:10.587
I had to kind of say I don't
know how else to do it now, guys.

00:15:10.587 --> 00:15:11.420
It feels like I was lying down

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:14.487
for so many hours for two whole episodes.

00:15:14.487 --> 00:15:16.184
I remember I fell asleep

00:15:16.184 --> 00:15:19.735
in the middle of a scene and woke up.

00:15:19.735 --> 00:15:20.568
You know when you wake up

00:15:20.568 --> 00:15:22.022
and you don't know quite where you are?

00:15:22.022 --> 00:15:23.693
There's nothing scarier than waking up

00:15:23.693 --> 00:15:25.331
in the middle of Game of Thrones world

00:15:25.331 --> 00:15:27.503
naked and everyone standing over you.

00:15:27.503 --> 00:15:28.810
I think oh my God,

00:15:28.810 --> 00:15:31.830
I've died and I actually
ended up in Westeros.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.524
- [Interviewer] Can you speak
a little about the journey

00:15:34.524 --> 00:15:38.906
that you've been on with Jon
Snow throughout these seasons?

00:15:38.906 --> 00:15:40.489
- Wow, it's um,

00:15:41.970 --> 00:15:44.469
it's been an incredible journey.

00:15:44.469 --> 00:15:46.403
It's been a journey all
through my twenties,

00:15:46.403 --> 00:15:48.156
all through his twenties.

00:15:48.156 --> 00:15:50.573
We've sort of grown up together.

00:15:50.573 --> 00:15:53.223
It'll be very hard letting
someone like that go.

00:15:53.223 --> 00:15:56.390
I'll always have an affinity with him.

00:15:58.471 --> 00:15:59.304
I've loved him.

00:15:59.304 --> 00:16:00.137
I love playing him.

00:16:00.137 --> 00:16:01.833
I love being part of the series.

00:16:01.833 --> 00:16:03.987
It's something that will be

00:16:03.987 --> 00:16:06.157
one of the most significant
things in my entire life.

00:16:06.157 --> 00:16:07.200
I'll miss the camaraderie.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:09.657
I'll miss the going back,

00:16:09.657 --> 00:16:13.092
like an office job that's
the best office in the world,

00:16:13.092 --> 00:16:14.925
once every six months.

00:16:15.888 --> 00:16:17.596
I really will miss that.

00:16:17.596 --> 00:16:18.429
I'll miss the crew.

00:16:18.429 --> 00:16:20.961
I'll miss everyone who works on the show.

00:16:20.961 --> 00:16:22.794
Yeah, that'll be hard.

